{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode/pulls/343670","id":4976593217,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAn8RLM8AAAABKKDJQQ","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/pull/343670","diff_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/pull/343670.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/pull/343670.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode/issues/343670","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode/pulls/343670/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode/pulls/343670/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode/issues/343670/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode/statuses/e854b46f8949c8e327ce60f4885525e8b1499a75","number":343670,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"dialogs: fix typed Windows drive-root navigation","user":{"login":"roblourens","id":323878,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzg3OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323878?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens","html_url":"https://github.com/roblourens","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"body":"<!-- Thank you for submitting a Pull Request. Please:\n* Read our Pull Request guidelines:\n  https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/wiki/How-to-Contribute#pull-requests\n* Associate an issue with the Pull Request.\n* Ensure that the code is up-to-date with the `main` branch.\n* Include a description of the proposed changes and how to test them.\n-->\n\nFix typing a Windows drive root in the simple file dialog, including when browsing a Windows Mission Control environment from macOS.\n\nWhile entering `Q:\\` character by character, the picker can navigate to the synthetic filesystem root after `Q`. The direct-child filtering optimization then treats `Q:\\` as a filename filter because `hasTrailingPathSeparator` intentionally excludes drive-root separators. Check the input's actual trailing separator instead, so a complete drive root navigates while incomplete `Q:` input still filters.\n\nAdds regression coverage for `Q:\\`, `Q:/`, and `Q:`. The affected condition was introduced in #330629. No filesystem grants or sharing permissions change.\n\nTo test, connect to a Windows environment with a second drive, open its folder picker, replace the current path by typing `Q:\\` character by character, and verify that the second drive's folders appear. This failed before the change and passed afterward in an isolated macOS Code OSS client connected to the existing Windows VS Code host; pasting the complete path also worked. The original URI-less permission-denied log entries were not conclusively attributed to this picker bug.\n\nLocal checks: `fnm exec --using 24.22.0 npm run build-fast -- --client-only` passed; `fnm exec --using 24.22.0 ./scripts/test.sh --run src/vs/workbench/services/dialogs/test/browser/simpleFileDialog.test.ts --reporter dot` passed (17 tests); `fnm exec --using 24.22.0 npm run eslint -- src/vs/workbench/services/dialogs/browser/simpleFileDialog.ts src/vs/workbench/services/dialogs/test/browser/simpleFileDialog.test.ts` passed.\n\n(Written by Copilot)\n","labels":[],"milestone":{"id":18616028,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAn8RLM4BHA